Unity: 6000.4.7f1
Scene: Assets/Scenes/PrototypeBootstrapHost.unity
Date: 2026-05-23

Root-cause diagnosis:
- The visible-ship regression fits the Functional Blender / weapon binder path, not the camera jitter/performance path.
- The scene had serialized allowGeneratedFallbackWhenImportedAssetMissing = 0 while PrototypeBootstrap could suppress generated fallback after an imported binding failure.
- PrototypeFunctionalShipBinder treated visible turret yaw/pitch renderer failures as missing required functional sockets for the whole ship.
- PrototypeShipVisualSwitcher hid generated primitives before proving that the imported visual had an active enabled renderer.

Implemented visibility policy:
- PrototypeBootstrapHost.unity: allowGeneratedFallbackWhenImportedAssetMissing = 1.
- Bootstrap now treats imported flight socket failure as a visible-ship safety fallback even if the old scene flag is false.
- Functional binder now reports:
  - hasRequiredFlightSockets
  - hasRequiredWeaponSockets
  - hasRequiredVisibleWeaponRenderers
  - hasVisibleImportedShip
- Missing visible turret renderers degrade weapon visuals only; they no longer fail the whole ship spawn.
- Visual clone safety now validates clone renderers before hiding original turret visuals.
- VisualSwitcher now hides generated primitives only after the imported visual has an active enabled renderer.

